# Single-Module Code Style Guide

Base package: `com.mascill.healthtrack`

## Package Naming

```kotlin
com.mascill.healthtrack.data
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.datasource.local
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.datasource.remote
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.mapper
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.model.request
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.model.response
com.mascill.healthtrack.data.repository
com.mascill.healthtrack.domain.model
com.mascill.healthtrack.domain.repository
com.mascill.healthtrack.domain.usecase
com.mascill.healthtrack.presentation.home
com.mascill.healthtrack.di
com.mascill.healthtrack.util
```

Do not add `data/service/` (Retrofit) for Supabase CRUD. `data/model/entity/` holds Room entities. Preferences use DataStore (`healthtrack_prefs`), not Room.

## File Naming

| Type | File Name | Location |
|---|---|---|
| Domain Model | `Profile.kt` | `domain/model/` |
| Response | `ProfileResponse.kt` | `data/model/response/` |
| Request | `ProfileOnboardingRequest.kt` | `data/model/request/` |
| Remote DataSource | `ProfileRemoteDataSource.kt` | `data/datasource/remote/` |
| Repository Interface | `ProfileRepository.kt` | `domain/repository/` |
| Repository Impl | `ProfileRepositoryImpl.kt` | `data/repository/` |
| UseCase | `CompleteOnboardingUseCase.kt` | `domain/usecase/` |
| ViewModel | `HomeViewModel.kt` | `presentation/home/` |
| Screen | `HomeScreen.kt` | `presentation/home/` |
| UI State | `HomeUIState.kt` | `presentation/home/model/` |
| Component | `UserCard.kt` | `presentation/home/component/` |
| Shared Component | `LoadingIndicator.kt` | `presentation/common/component/` |

## Class Naming Conventions

```kotlin
data class Profile(val id: String, val userId: String)

@Serializable
data class ProfileResponse(
    val id: String,
    @SerialName("user_id") val userId: String,
)

interface ProfileRepository {
    suspend fun getProfile(): Result<Profile>
}

class ProfileRepositoryImpl @Inject constructor(
    private val remote: ProfileRemoteDataSource,
    private val dispatcher: AppDispatcher,
) : ProfileRepository

class GetProfileUseCase @Inject constructor(
    private val repository: ProfileRepository,
)

@HiltViewModel
class HomeViewModel @Inject constructor(...)

@Composable
fun HomeScreen(...)

data class HomeUIState(...)
```

DTOs use `@Serializable` / `@SerialName`, **not** Moshi `@Json`.

## Function Naming

```kotlin
fun ProfileResponse.toProfile(): Profile
fun MutableList<NavKey>.navigateToHome()
fun onSubmitClick()
fun loadData()

@Composable fun HomeScreen()
@Composable private fun ContentSection()
```

## Constants

URL, publishable key, and Google client id live in `BuildConfig` from `local.properties`. **Never** put them in `Constants.kt` or git.

```kotlin
object Constants {
    const val TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30L

    object Prefs {
        const val NAME = "healthtrack_prefs"
        const val KEY_THEME_MODE = "theme_mode"
    }

    object Tables {
        const val PROFILES = "profiles"
    }
}
```

## Compose Dimensions

```kotlin
private const val SCREEN_PADDING = 16
private const val ITEM_SPACING = 8

@Composable
fun MyScreen() {
    Column(
        modifier = Modifier.padding(SCREEN_PADDING.dp),
        verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(ITEM_SPACING.dp),
    ) { ... }
}
```

## Documentation

Public types and functions need KDoc (Detekt). Do not add new issues to `detekt-baseline.xml`.

```kotlin
/**
 * Repository for learner profile operations.
 */
interface ProfileRepository {
    /**
     * One-shot fetch of the current user's profile.
     */
    suspend fun getProfile(): Result<Profile>
}
```

## Result Handling

```kotlin
suspend fun getProfile(): Result<Profile>

repository.getProfile()
    .onSuccess { profile -> /* handle success */ }
    .onFailure { error -> /* map to AppError in presentation */ }
```

User-facing errors: `AppError` in `presentation/common/model`, not copy per screen.

## Trailing Commas

Enabled for git diffs.

## Import Rules

- No wildcard imports
- Organize imports alphabetically within groups
- Remove unused imports
- `io.github.jan.supabase` only under `data/` and `di/`
